// Call-site arena promotion.
//
// `alloc_and_return` hands fresh storage back to its caller, so on its own the
// classifier would have to call it escaping and let it fall back to the general
// allocator. The caller is the one that knows the answer: `main` prints the value
// and lets the binding die with the frame, so the storage never leaves it.
//
// Every call to the callee bounds the result, which is what lets the callee's
// signature gain the arena handle. `main` creates the arena once, passes it, and
// releases the whole chunk on the way out; the callee fills it instead of calling
// the general allocator.
int* function alloc_and_return() {
    var node = memory.allocate<int>(8);
    node[0] = 42;
    return node;
}

int function main() {
    var n = alloc_and_return();
    print(n[0]);
    return 0;
}
